{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Interim RCA/update: live host checks found review-bot webhook 401s from Gerrit container IP 172.21.0.4 after the token rotation, while SSM, compose .env, running review-bot env, and rebar.git refs/meta/config:webhooks.config now all hash to the same token (03a77b8c96ff...). Gerrit was restarted at 2026-09-09T12:50:31Z; review-bot at 12:20:18Z. Working hypothesis: the stale-secret interval was a Gerrit/webhooks reload gap during rotation; the class fix is to make inbound webhook auth rejects observable instead of allowing /review/health to stay green. RED evidence: new tests failed because /health lacked webhook_auth_rejections and observability.sh published no reviewbot_webhook_auth_rejections metric. GREEN targeted evidence so far: review-bot app/script/alarm tests pass (159 passed targeted)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788958890460864001,"uuid":"12e20133-f7ce-44d4-bdfa-26aa9a26647f"}